laurel (Mi A3, iOS 26): tu_cs_reset frees all BOs of a command stream but the last, so a command buffer that grew makes them again after each reset: a kernel buffer, a map, a free per frame. RedwoodGPU boot 16 with live glass: 650 to 683 buffers made in 5 s, 680 to 1385 us each, while the kernel keeps nothing under 256 KiB.
A reset CS keeps up to 8 BOs per array and takes them at its next growth. A command buffer is reset only after the GPU is done with it. Applied by scripts/gpu/turnip-build.sh (TU_EXTRA_PATCHES). [V] code path, compiled; effect on the count: next boot.

--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cs.h	2026-11-03 03:01:15.224352563 +0530
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cs.h	2026-11-03 03:01:40.128173218 +0530
@@ -76,6 +76,9 @@
    uint32_t bo_count;
    uint32_t bo_capacity;
    uint32_t *start;
+   /* laurel: BOs kept over a reset, for the next growth of this CS */
+   struct tu_bo *spare[8];
+   uint32_t spare_count;
 };
 
 #define TU_COND_EXEC_STACK_SIZE 4
